{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Tally (docs/tally.md, ADR 0013). 'match': where a sample goes. A sample is a 'platform' (android or windows), an 'app' (package or executable) and on Windows a 'title'. The owner's 'own' rules come first, then 'defaults' in order (the whole of contracts/content/tally-rules.json when 'defaults' is \"shipped\"); the first match wins, nothing matched is 'other'. An 'app' rule is the whole name ignoring case; a 'title' rule is contained in the title ignoring case, on Windows only; a 'folder' rule is the name of the folder an editor's title names, ignoring case; a rule's 'platform' is android, windows or any. On Windows a rule's own 'project' wins, otherwise the editor's folder names the project (see 'project'); on Android there is never a project. A folder rule never matches when there is no editor folder, or when its pattern names no folder. 'folder': the folder an editor's title names: Visual Studio Code (code.exe) the part before ' - Visual Studio Code' and after the last other ' - ', Android Studio (studio64.exe) the part before the first ' \u2013 ', Visual Studio (devenv.exe) the part before ' - Microsoft Visual Studio' without a trailing '(...)'; a leading '\u25cf' (unsaved) and spaces are dropped; anything else is null. 'project': the one project whose local folder's last part is that folder name, ignoring case; none when no project or several have it. 'idle': whether the clock runs: never while 'locked' or 'asleep', and not once 'secondsSinceInput' reaches 300, unless the category is 'video'. 'days': a device's 'intervals' (local times) as planning-day totals: each interval is cut where a planning day starts ('startHour'), time two intervals share counts once for the one that started first, and each day, category and project gets its seconds rounded to the nearest minute (half a minute rounds up), at most 1440; days with no minutes are left out, the rest ordered by day, category, then project (none first). 'ids': a tally day's id is a UUID version 5 of 'tally/<owner, lower case>/<day>/<device, lower case>/<category>/<project or ->' in 'namespace'. 'weeks': the stats block, the 'count' weeks (the apps show 12) ending with the week holding 'today' (weeks start on Monday), oldest first, each with its minutes and each category's, most first, then by category; rows are kept by 'kind' (phone, pc, or null for both) and 'category' (or null for all), and a week with nothing is there with 0 minutes and no categories. Every device's minutes add up. The next three are worked out on the device from its own raw record and never sync (the Tally place's day and apps). 'window': what an app row shows under it: an editor's folder (as 'folder'), or a browser's site (chrome.exe, msedge.exe, firefox.exe, brave.exe, opera.exe, vivaldi.exe, arc.exe): the title cut at ' - ', ' | ', ' · ', ' – ' and ' — ', the last part (the browser's name) dropped and the part before it kept, without a leading count like '(3) '; a title with nothing before the browser's name, any other app and no title are null. 'hours': a device's 'stretches' (local times, already sorted into a category) as the 24 hours of the planning 'day', from 'startHour' on (so with 4, the last hours are 00 to 03 of the next date); time two stretches share counts once for the one that started first, and each hour has its seconds and each category's, most first, then by category. 'expect' lists only the hours with time; the others are there with 0 seconds and no categories. 'apps': the stretches from the planning day 'from' to 'to', both included, cut where those days start and end and with shared time counted once as in 'hours', by category, then app (its name trimmed and in lower case), then 'window'; each level's seconds rounded to the nearest minute (half a minute rounds up) and left out at 0, ordered most first, then by category, app or label; an app's 'windows' hold only the time that has a label.",
  "namespace": "b8c61b22-5e0c-4f0a-9d1e-6f4a2c7e3b91",
